<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/maven-v4_0_0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
    <parent>
        <groupId>com.fiscaladmin.joget</groupId>
        <artifactId>joget-platform-plugins</artifactId>
        <version>1.0.0</version>
        <relativePath>../../pom.xml</relativePath>
    </parent>
    <groupId>com.fiscaladmin.joget</groupId>
    <artifactId>joget-transition-guard</artifactId>
    <!-- 1.3.0 (METHOD-2026-10-08-07): a set-now field marked @date is written as the day alone,
         and an applied move writes the rows its `audit` and `notify` properties name. A minor
         step: two optional keys added, nothing an existing configuration says reads otherwise.
         1.4.0 (METHOD-2026-10-08-11): a guard term none(<entity> where <condition>) counts another
         record's rows (`records`, `thisKey`), and an applied move sets columns on a related
         record's rows (`related`). A minor step: three optional keys added; a guard with no
         none(...) term reads as before.
         1.5.0 (METHOD-2026-10-12-14; the owner's ruling of 11 October 2026 on round 1, card 4):
         a refused move writes the history entries and alerts its `refused` property names. A
         minor step: one optional key added; an applied move writes exactly what it wrote.
         1.6.0 (METHOD-2026-10-16-01; MT-DM's request of 15 October 2026): MoveRefusal, a form
         validator that judges a move before its act is saved and says a refusal in the model's own
         words; a move withheld from the person the record names (`withheld`); a set-now field
         marked @actor written with who made the move. A minor step: one optional key and one
         mark added, and a new plugin; a configuration that uses none of them reads as before.
         1.7.0 (METHOD-2026-11-03-13; MT-DM's hand-off of 22 October 2026, items 1 and 3): no
         refused move ends on "Form Submitted" - MoveRefusal refuses a failed term the model gives
         no words before the save, in words drawn from the guard (the move's name, `moveName`, and
         the term, filled from the record), and leaves to the root guard the term it already asks
         (`rootAsks`); a column of a history entry or an alert may hold `words`, the words a
         refusal was said in, never a code. A minor step: two optional keys and one source added;
         a model whose every failed term has words, or whose moves have no guard, reads as before.
         1.8.0 (MT-DM DM3-2026-10-27-159, the alerts' words): an alert points at its template and
         shows its words - where `templates` names where the templates are kept
         (form>table>nameColumn>contentColumn), a column may hold `template_key`, the identifier of
         the template row the notify names, and `content`, that row's content with its merge fields
         filled from the move and the record moved. A minor step: one optional key and two sources
         added; a configuration that uses none of them reads as before.
         1.9.0 (METHOD-2026-11-05-45; MT-DM's hand-off of 8 November 2026, item 46): the rows the
         guard writes and changes carry the columns the platform fills when it saves a form's row,
         by the rule of AppServiceImpl.storeFormData (Joget 9.0.7, lines 2161-2196): a history entry
         or an alert it makes (and a refusal's, from MoveRefusal) takes dateCreated, dateModified
         and the who-columns; the record moved, the target and the act saved, and the rows a
         `related` line sets take dateModified and modifiedBy / modifiedByName, their created three
         kept as loaded and filled only where the row holds no dateCreated. The move's instant is
         read once, and its moment and every stamp are that reading in the JVM's zone. A move with
         no person (an empty name, or the platform's roleAnonymous) is made by `system`, in the
         history, the status event and the @actor mark; the stamps keep the platform's own value.
         A minor step: no key added; the moments, words, codes and moves read as before.
         1.10.0 (METHOD-2026-11-05-51, R34; MT-DM's answer of 8 November 2026 to item 46's acceptance):
         the status event a move appends through StatusManager.apply is stamped as the platform
         stamps a row (joget-event-chain 2.1.0), and the guard hands that call the move's own
         instant, so the event, the history entry and the rows the move writes are one reading.
         The pins of joget-event-chain and joget-status-manager move to 2.1.0. A minor step: no key
         added; the moments, words, codes and moves read as before. -->
    <version>1.10.0</version>
    <packaging>bundle</packaging>
    <name>joget-transition-guard</name>
    <description>Generic config-driven lifecycle transition guard (form post-processor -> StatusManager).</description>
    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.felix</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-bundle-plugin</artifactId>
                <extensions>true</extensions>
                <configuration>
                    <instructions>
                        <Export-Package></Export-Package>
                        <Private-Package>{local-packages}</Private-Package>
                        <Bundle-Activator>com.fiscaladmin.joget.transitionguard.Activator</Bundle-Activator>
                        <Import-Package>!*,com.fiscaladmin.joget.eventchain,com.fiscaladmin.joget.statusmanager,org.joget.commons.util,org.joget.plugin.base,org.joget.plugin.property.model,org.joget.apps.app.service,org.joget.apps.form.dao,org.joget.apps.form.model,org.joget.apps.form.service,org.joget.directory.model,org.joget.directory.model.service,org.joget.workflow.util,org.osgi.framework;version="1.3.0"</Import-Package>
                        <Embed-Dependency>*;scope=compile;inline=false</Embed-Dependency>
                        <Embed-Transitive>false</Embed-Transitive>
                        <DynamicImport-Package>*</DynamicImport-Package>
                    </instructions>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.fiscaladmin.joget</groupId>
            <artifactId>joget-event-chain</artifactId>
            <version>2.1.0</version>
            <scope>provided</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.fiscaladmin.joget</groupId>
            <artifactId>joget-status-manager</artifactId>
            <version>2.1.0</version>
            <scope>provided</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.joget</groupId>
            <artifactId>wflow-core</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>javax.servlet</groupId>
            <artifactId>javax.servlet-api</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <!-- METHOD-2026-09-25-04, item 5: the guard's first tests (target mode, roles) -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>junit</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.mockito</groupId>
            <artifactId>mockito-core</artifactId>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>
</project>
